## Browser Audio Recording Notes

I got excited about this and took some notes about our options here:

- https://stackblitz.com/edit/react-voice-visualizer?file=README.md
- https://collab-project.github.io/videojs-record/#/usage, mostly dead but not completely https://ossinsight.io/analyze/collab-project/videojs-record#commits. Started 2016
- https://howlerjs.com just for playing audio
- https://github.com/muaz-khan/RecordRTC no updates in 3yrs, lots of commits, but recent commits
- https://github.com/maklov/react-mic completely dead
- https://github.com/vocaroo/simple-audio-recorder?tab=readme-ov-file recently created, but looks mostly dead
- https://github.com/YZarytskyi/react-voice-visualizer/issues/30 is the best one I could find

# Developer Notes: Audio-only Recording System

## Overview
**Platform:** Addpipe
**Purpose:** Enable in-app audio recording with incremental capture and automatic storage.

## Key Features
- **Audio-only Mode:** Available on desktop and mobile.
- **React Integration:** Use @addpipe/react-pipe-media-recorder from npm.
- **Incremental Saving:** Streams recordings to servers in real-time; recovers recordings if connection fails.

## Pricing
- **Audio-only:** $0.01/min
- **Standard Plan:** $50/month for 5000 minutes
- **PRO Plan:** $250/month

## Additional Notes
- Forwarded to John Clemente and David Laprade for future development considerations.
- Screenshot of pricing details attached.
